// Load buffering where only Strengthening breaks the cycle. MoRDor's own test,
// after the strengthening example of sMRD (Richards et al., OOPSLA 2025,
// Appendix C).
//
// Thread 1 writes y := 1 when r1 = 1, and when r1 != 1 and r2 = 1. sMRD's
// Strengthening (Definition 4.11) may conjoin r2 = 1 to the first write's
// predicate, since the read of z is po-before it. The two writes then lift
// into (r2 = 1) |- W y 1, which depends on the read of z and no longer on the
// read of x. Nothing orders z := 1 after the read of y in thread 2, so
// dp ∪ ppo ∪ rf has no cycle and sMRD allows r1 = 1 && r2 = 1 && ry = 1.
//
// MoRDor strengthens only with the equation between the values of two
// conflicting writes, as part of Lifting (Elaborations.StrengthenLiftElab).
// Here both write 1, so there is no equation to add, the writes keep their
// dependency on the read of x, and the outcome is forbidden. This records the
// restriction; docs/DEPARTURES.md lists it. RC11 forbids the outcome: po ∪ rf
// is cyclic.
x := 0; y := 0; z := 0;
{
  r1 := x;
  r2 := z;
  if (r1 = 1) {
    y := 1
  } else {
    if (r2 = 1) { y := 1 }
  }
} ||| {
  z := 1;
  ry := y;
  x := ry
}
%%
forbid (r1 = 1 && r2 = 1 && ry = 1) [sMRD, RC11]
